closeout statement: a concurrent worker claimed bitumen-canophilic-pekingese after that read and began the six-file comment-only implementation in the provisioned worktree. The ticket is now in_progress, and the worktree contains uncommitted edits confined to its declared paths. Preserve those edits. The worker must finish or park them under the closeout instruction, and no Gerrit push is allowed before a non-author exact-candidate matrix passes.","timestamp":1789057710329631001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Candidate commit cb575290845440e74c579d1ebfba0a9b945732e9 changes exactly the six declared infra/compose files with 213 inserted and 770 deleted lines, all standalone comments or adjacent blanks. A stronger line-by-line comparison confirms every non-comment configuration or executable line and each Docker syntax directive are byte-exact. Green evidence at this SHA includes config-check, 299 focused tests with 23 expected skips, repository lint, repository typecheck, diff --check, comment-policy punctuation scan, and commit-ticket verification. The initial focused run had one failure because test_reviewbot_entrypoint.py consumes the literal '# Data-capture entrypoint' anchor; the anchor was restored in the condensed block and the full focused rerun passed. Append-only verification correction: the persisted preserve-executable-lines command uses escaped basic-regex grouping, but git diff --ignore-matching-lines parses an extended regular expression. The persisted spelling exits 1 on comment-only diffs; the syntax-correct equivalent with unescaped grouping and alternation exits 0, and the stronger independent line comparison also passes. Per operator direction, no full local test suite was run. Awaiting non-author exact-candidate semantic and bloat-removal review before any Gerrit push.","timestamp":1789058441737292001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Candidate SHA correction: before any push, cb575290845440e74c579d1ebfba0a9b945732e9 was amended to 4b1e877ae62de0253f1bd562db3b0f4273034353. The amendment keeps the moved auto-push rationale inside its original review-bot environment comment block instead of creating an addition-only block. No configuration line or substantive fact changed. The exact executable/configuration comparison, syntax-correct diff guard, config-check, diff integrity, pre-commit gate, Change-Id, DCO sign-off, and ticket trailer pass on 4b1e877ae62de0253f1bd562db3b0f4273034353. This SHA is the only candidate an independent reviewer should cite.","timestamp":1789058690483187001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Exact-candidate validation update: the complete focused selection was rerun after the final amendment at 4b1e877ae62de0253f1bd562db3b0f4273034353 and passed with 299 tests passed and 23 expected skips in 179.09 seconds. No failure or warning remained. The candidate is clean and still unpushed pending its non-author matrix.","timestamp":1789059148638652001}],"created_at":1788570445871225746,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7ad6c440-b404-4bb6-9d5f-116053384e88","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"7215-d8d9-6ce2-4b50"},{"link_uuid":"63bd2889-3c02-4ada-b523-64060ad9c1ec","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5bad-2369-2d4a-44e9"},{"link_uuid":"1505c040-5252-483b-9a2e-77954938d9a5","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"b60c-ece3-8baa-4eb3"},{"link_uuid":"787b92a0-5924-4283-88c6-1b137bdd7214","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"f512-85a3-31d2-4470"},{"link_uuid":"1d5e34dc-65ef-48a4-892e-8cf1beb85bb2","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"ea72-4b04-fa5e-4cb7"},{"link_uuid":"fe15482d-4322-4bfc-80dd-8651161a43f3","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"bdba-1839-5341-44df"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe six `infra/compose` files below contain repeated, obvious, or historical prose identified by the comment audit and revalidated on `origin/main` at `c019920390926d543a0813d4c0c8721543d98776`. The remediation must shorten comments without weakening operational or security contracts.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only standalone comments and blank lines in the declared files. Preserve executable/configuration text byte-for-byte. Replace incident history and narration with the minimum current rationale needed by each consumer. Before the first Gerrit push, a reviewer who did not author the remediation must inspect the exact candidate commit and persist the complete semantic-preservation and bloat-removal matrix on a leaf-linked session log.\n\n## Scope\n- `docker-compose.yml` — Preserve the four-service topology and host-side nginx boundary; Gerrit external bind-volume persistence, `down -v` safety, loopback HTTP/public SSH, and journald consumption; review-bot bounded shutdown/store lock, proxy trust boundary, persistent ticket/signing mounts, UID-mismatch `safe.directory`, paired regions, three model slots/no legacy model variable, usage logs, scratch watermark/admission-marker ordering, and reporting-only healthcheck; opcert authoritative/no-push/external-key/loopback posture; MCP fail-closed non-loopback auth/Host/Origin, stop grace, persistent read-write tickets and blobless code clones, paired regions, soft-degrade PAT/Jira inputs versus fail-closed auth/key files, healthcheck, and parity with `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:mcp_run_new`. Consumers: Compose, deploy/observability scripts, security and operators.\n- `Dockerfile.gerrit` — Preserve in-image Python/g2p for Gerrit hooks, Python >=3.11 assertion, exact g2p commit because PyPI lacks compact-ID support, all three hook symlinks, secret exclusion, and final UID 1000. Consumers: image build, hook materialization, Gerrit operators.\n- `Dockerfile.mcp` — Preserve OpenSSH >=8.9 for SSHSIG; architecture/version/checksum-pinned ACLI; locked `agents,mcp,bedrock` install with uv-pin parity; unauthenticated loopback health endpoint; and the real entrypoint for persistent tickets/blobless code stores with soft clone failure. The image intentionally has no `USER` directive and runs as root. Consumers: image build, MCP startup and Jira mutation paths.\n- `Dockerfile.opcert` — Preserve OpenSSH >=8.9, locked `agents,reviewbot` install with uv-pin parity, externally mounted signing key, absence of boto3/SSM application runtime, and fixed uvicorn entrypoint. The image intentionally has no `USER` directive and runs as root. Consumers: trusted op-cert image and operators.\n- `Dockerfile.reviewbot` — Preserve root-context `.dockerignore` secret/debris exclusion, OpenSSH authorship signing, architecture-aware gitleaks, isolated/offline semgrep, locked explicit `agents,reviewbot,bedrock` install with uv-pin parity, writable-store helper, soft-failure persistent-ticket entrypoint, and root-mounted uvicorn endpoint. The image runs as root, matching Compose. Consumers: image build, scanners, review-bot startup and operators.\n- `gerrit.config` — Preserve canonical URL/basePath/serverId; proxy/listener/request logging; SSH/thread bounds; heap/JDK-21/off-heap limits; fail-closed OAuth prerequisites with secret separation; Lucene/NoteDb and signed-push posture; whole-topic collision warning; explicit mail disablement and restart requirement. Consumers: Gerrit, `compose-up.sh`, autodeploy signaling and operators.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes only standalone comments or blank lines in the six declared files.\n- [ ] Before the first Gerrit push, every Scope constraint and consumer contract has a PASS row with concrete before/after citations against the exact candidate commit in a leaf-linked session log authored by a reviewer who did not write the remediation.\n- [ ] Every edited comment block has an independent `bloat-removal` PASS row confirming that redundant, obvious, duplicated, or historical prose was removed while current non-obvious rationale remained.\n- [ ] Focused infra/config tests, `git diff --check`, repository lint, and repository type checking pass at the leaf commit.\n- [ ] No missing or FAIL semantic-preservation row remains at closure.\n\n## Verification\nRun the persisted comment-only diff guard, focused infra/config checks, path-scoped `git diff --check`, worktree-venv `make lint`, and worktree-venv `make typecheck`. Semantic preservation is judged by the independent exact-candidate matrix. Delegate the full repository test suite to Gerrit `Verified` because this leaf changes comments and blank lines only.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/compose/Dockerfile.gerrit","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/compose/Dockerfile.opcert","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"infra/compose/gerrit.config","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","49ac-d7e5-f383-4d7f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"49ac-d7e5-f383-4d7f","parent_status_uuid":"06845599-e570-43f5-b0a1-0c59f20b753a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"a0f1-b86c-5199-4a42","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in infra/compose","verif